	"roles": {
		"icefisher": {"title": "Ice-fisher", "work": "nets",
			"intro": ["Mind the hole. People fall in it. People don't come out of it.", "{name}. I fish through the ice. The fish don't like it any more than I do."],
			"self": ["Cut the hole at dawn, sit till dusk, go home with three fish and no feeling in your feet. Best job in the world.",
				"My line went taut last winter and stayed taut. Whatever was on the other end, it was bigger than the hole."],
			"talk": ["The trick is to talk to the fish. Not out loud. They hate that.",
				"Lost an auger down the hole this morning. Third this winter. The fish are building something.",
				"My wife says I smell of fish. I say she does too, she's just used to it.",
				"Thin ice sings before it breaks. Learn the song and you'll live to be old and grumpy like me.",
				"Caught a pike yesterday with a ring in its belly. Nobody's claimed the ring. Or the finger.",
				"Some days I sit out there and think the whole sea's asleep under me, snoring.",
				"Worst part's not the cold. It's the gulls. They watch you. They wait."]},
		"trapper": {"title": "Trapper", "work": "forage",
			"intro": ["You came up the trail? Then you saw my snares. Good. You didn't step in any.", "{name}. I trap hares and I keep wolves off the town. One of those pays."],
			"self": ["The wolves on this island hunt in packs of six. I've counted seven tracks lately. I don't like the seventh.",
				"Read the snow and it'll tell you everything that walked past since the last fall. Most of it was hungry."],
			"talk": ["Wolves don't hate us. They just count us, same as I count them.",
				"Checked forty snares since dawn. Two hares and a very angry fox. The fox kept the snare.",
				"Hare stew again tonight. Hare stew every night. I dream in hare.",
				"Snow's too soft this week. Every track slumps till it looks like a bear's.",
				"My dog runs the line faster than me now. I think she lets me keep up out of pity.",
				"Never set a trap upwind of the castle road. Don't ask why. I asked once.",
				"Fresh snowfall's an empty page. By noon, something hungry has always written on it."]},
		"doctor": {"title": "Doctor", "work": "home",
			"intro": ["Frostbite? Let me see. No. Keep your boots on. I believe you.", "I'm {name}. Fevers, breaks, chilblains, and pirates who think snow is soft."],
			"self": ["The old doctor up the mountain taught me. She was ninety and threw scalpels when she was cross.",
				"Every winter someone eats the blue moss for a dare. Every winter I'm the one who stays up all night."],
			"talk": ["Half my patients are fishermen with frozen toes. The other half are their wives, with headaches.",
				"Willow bark, warm broth and a stern look. That cures most things up here.",
				"If you're going to fight in the snow, fall forward. Backs break. Faces just look bad.",
				"I've stitched three pirates this month. One paid me. One proposed. One stole my good needle.",
				"Wash your hands. Yes, in the cold water. No, it's not torture, it's medicine.",
				"Long nights make people sad. I prescribe the inn, a song and somebody's hand to hold.",
				"I'm short on bandages again. Bring me a torn sail some time and I'll make it useful."]},
		"furrier": {"title": "Furrier", "work": "market",
			"intro": ["Cold? Course you are. You dress like it's summer somewhere.", "{name}. Coats, hats, mittens. Everything between you and the wind."],
			"self": ["A good coat outlives the man wearing it. I've sold the same coat four times. It keeps coming back.",
				"Wolf for the collar, hare for the lining, wool for the rest. The bear's not for sale. The bear was a friend."],
			"talk": ["Sold a coat to a pirate who swore he'd never be cold. He came back next morning, blue.",
				"Stitching's slow work. Sixty stitches a cuff, and I count every one out loud.",
				"Wolf pelts are thin this year. The wolves are hungry too, so I don't complain to them.",
				"Every coat I make has a pocket nobody knows about. Not even the wearer. That's my secret.",
				"That hat? Hare. Two of them. They died for your ears, so wear it properly.",
				"Some captains ask for red fur. There's no red fur. There's fur, and dye, and lies.",
				"My needles get so cold they bite me. I bite them first now."]},
		"storyteller": {"title": "Storyteller", "work": "plaza",
			"intro": ["Another captain! Sit by the fire. I'll tell you how the last one froze. It's a good one.", "Old {name}. I keep the stories. Long winters need long stories."],
			"self": ["I've told the tale of the castle on the peak so often the children tell it back to me, wrong.",
				"When I was a girl the mountain still had a king. Now it has snow, and something that walks in it."],
			"talk": ["Every story I tell is true. I just decide which parts.",
				"The children want monsters. The old folk want love stories. The drunks want both at once.",
				"I lost my voice for a week last winter. The town nearly went mad from the quiet.",
				"Bring me a new tale from the sea, Captain, and I'll trade you two old ones. Fair price.",
				"The fire pops at the best parts. I swear it listens. I've been telling it stories sixty years.",
				"Some nights I tell the one about the frozen king, and the wind outside goes still to hear it.",
				"My memory's going, they say. Rubbish. I just remember things that haven't happened yet."]},
		"watcher": {"title": "Lookout", "work": "nets",
			"intro": ["Saw your sails through the snow at dawn. Thought you were a ghost ship. You still might be.", "{name}. I watch the pack ice. It moves, you know. Nobody believes me."],
			"self": ["On a clear night you can see the castle lights from the harbour wall. Nobody's lit them in years.",
				"Three kinds of ship come through the ice: traders, fools and wrecks. Usually in that order."],
			"talk": ["Count the bergs at dawn, count them at dusk. If the numbers don't match, something moved them.",
				"My eyes are good. My knees are ruined. Ninety steps up that wall, twice a day.",
				"Saw a whale break the ice last spring. Saw a ship try it too. Only the whale managed.",
				"A spyglass is a lonely friend. It shows you everything and keeps none of it warm.",
				"When the horizon goes white and the sky goes white, I ring the bell. That's a blizzard. Go inside.",
				"Folk ask what I'm looking for out there. Honestly? Somebody out there looking back."]},
		"brewer": {"title": "Brewer", "work": "market",
			"intro": ["Something warm? Course you want something warm. Everyone wants something warm.", "{name}. I brew the cider. Hot, spiced, strong enough to thaw an anchor."],
			"self": ["Apples, cloves, a kettle and patience. The apples come off the ships. The patience is all mine.",
				"A pirate once traded his sword for a barrel of my cider. He came back next winter for another barrel. Without a sword."],
			"talk": ["The secret's the cloves. No, the cinnamon. I tell everyone a different secret.",
				"Kettle's been on the boil since autumn. If it stops, the town riots. I'm not exaggerating.",
				"I tried brewing with snow water once. Tasted like a cold morning. Not in a good way.",
				"Every cask has a name. That one's Grumbles. Strong and bitter, like my uncle.",
				"Sold my first mug at nine years old. Got tipsy on my second at ten. That's how you learn a trade.",
				"If a ship's late, I brew extra. Sailors who've been in the ice drink like the sea owes them."]},
	},
	"barks": {
		"day": ["Cold one today. They're all cold ones.", "Snow's coming. Snow's always coming.", "Keep moving. Stand still too long and the frost gets ideas.",
			"Ships come, ships go. Most of them come back with ice on the rigging.", "Don't walk on the lake. Nobody listens. Don't walk on the lake.", "You can see the peak today. That's bad luck, the old ones say.",
			"Sun's up for four hours today. Make them count.", "Morning! Mind the drift by the door, it ate a goat last week.",
			"Breath freezes in your beard by noon. Mine's half icicle.", "Wood's running low. Someone's going up with an axe. Not me.",
			"Bright out. Squint or go snow-blind, your choice.", "The ice groaned all morning. Means the sea's turning over.",
			"Hot cider at midday keeps the joints moving. Doctor's orders. Mine.", "Another ship in? The harbour's busier than the graveyard. Barely.",
			"Clear sky, no wind. Something's wrong.", "Wolves were in the square at dawn. Took a boot. Just the one.",
			"A pirate in a summer shirt. Now I've seen everything.", "The castle's got a crow on its tower today. Big as a dog.",
			"Kids built a snow captain by the pier. Better hat than yours."],
		"evening": ["The inn's the only warm place left on this island.", "Another day the mountain didn't come down on us. Drink to that.", "Sun's going. Keep to the lamps.",
			"Listen. Hear that? That's the wolves, finding their voices.",
			"Shutters closed, fire stoked. Evening's a job like any other.", "The sky goes green some evenings. The old ones call it the king's cloak.",
			"Supper's fish. Supper's always fish. I'd fight a bear for an onion.", "Bring the dogs in. The cold comes down off the peak at dusk.",
			"Last light on the castle. Pretty, if you don't know the stories.", "That's the inn bell. Means the cider's hot and the fiddler's sober.",
			"Long night coming. Sixteen hours of it. Bring a book.", "Mind the steps going home. They freeze the moment the sun's off them.",
			"Lamplighter's late again. Probably asleep in a drift, the fool.", "Dusk is when the hares come out. And whatever eats hares.",
			"Count your crew before dark. The snow doesn't give them back.", "Ice on the harbour's turning blue. Cold night ahead.",
			"Evening, Captain. Your nose is the colour of a cherry.", "My feet thawed at last. Just in time to freeze again tonight.",
			"Somebody's singing at the inn. Badly. Very badly. Go and help."],
		"night": ["Keep to the lamps after dark. The snow hides holes, and worse.", "Can't sleep. Something big walking on the ridge.",
			"Shh. The crystals are bright tonight. Something's stirring under them.",
			"Stars are so sharp tonight you could cut yourself on them.", "Who's out at this hour? Oh. A pirate. Of course.",
			"Wolves are close tonight. Hear them answering each other?", "My candle's the last one lit on the street. I like it that way.",
			"The castle lit up last night. Just for a breath. Then gone.", "Cold enough to crack the bell. It's happened. Twice.",
			"Go to bed, Captain. Nothing good's awake this late.", "I heard footsteps on my roof. Snow doesn't have footsteps.",
			"Night watch. Me, a lantern and a flask of cider. Mostly cider.", "Sky's dancing green again. Make a wish. Not out loud.",
			"Midnight, and the sea's frozen still. You could hear a fish blink.", "Don't follow the lights on the ice. They're not lanterns.",
			"That's not the wind howling. The wind doesn't stop to breathe.", "Numb fingers, numb toes, long shift. Wake me at dawn.",
			"Snow's falling sideways tonight. Blizzard by morning, you watch.", "Inn's still lit. Someone's losing at cards and won't admit it."],
		"nets": ["Ice is thick this week. Good for walking, bad for fishing.", "Hand me that auger. No, the sharp one.", "Every fish through this hole is a little miracle. A cold, wet miracle.",
			"Bite's slow. Fish are deep and sulking.", "Don't stamp. You'll scare them all the way to the next island.",
			"Pulled up a boot this morning. Kept it. Good boot.", "Hole's skinned over again. Pass the pick."],
		"forage": ["Hare tracks. Fresh. Quiet now.", "Wolf sign. Old. Probably. Keep your voice down anyway.", "Good pine nuts under this one. Help me dig, or move on.",
			"Snare's sprung and empty. Clever little thief.", "Lingonberries, under the snow. Frozen sweet. Try one.",
			"Stay on my tracks. The drifts here are deeper than you are tall.", "Pine sap for the doctor, bark for the tanner. Busy morning."],
		"dock": ["Tide's breaking the ice again. Everything's late when the ice breaks.", "Mind the planks. They're frozen. So are you, by the look of you.", "Your ship? She's got ice on her bow. Knock it off or she'll sit low.",
			"Lines are frozen stiff. Chip them before you cast off.", "Pack ice is drifting in. Don't moor long, Captain.",
			"Unloading salt and apples. Ships bring everything but warmth."],
		"boats": ["Every boat here's been hauled over the ice at least once. Most of them twice.", "Hand me that mallet. They're all mallets. That one.",
			"Tar won't set in this cold. Hull's patched with hope.", "She's frozen in to the gunwales. Spring will let her go.",
			"Runners on the keel. Up here, boats are half sledge.", "Caulking by lamplight. My fingers stopped arguing an hour ago."],
		"stall": ["Fresh this morning. Frozen this afternoon.", "Furs, fish, firewood. The three things a sailor needs here, in no order.",
			"Smoked eel! Keeps a month, warms a week!", "Mittens, two for one. Nobody's got just the one hand.",
			"Firewood by the armful. Dry, mostly. Dry-ish.", "Step up, step up. Cold stall, warm prices."],
		"market": ["Furs, smoked fish, a hat that fits most heads. What d'you need?", "Prices go up when the ice closes the harbour. Lucky you got in.", "Haggle all you like. My ears are frozen, I can't hear you.",
			"Walrus tusk, carved or raw. Lucky charms, the sailors say.", "Salt cod from the north shore. Fresh as anything up here gets.",
			"Coins are so cold they stick to the palm. Pay me quick."],
		"home": ["Roof's buried again. The roof's always buried.", "The little ones are sledging down by the pines. I hope.", "If you see a hare with a red ribbon, it's ours. Don't eat it.",
			"Door's frozen shut again. Kick it for me? Gently.", "Bread's rising by the stove. Only warm thing in the house.",
			"Shovel, shovel, shovel. Then it snows. Then shovel."],
		"plaza": ["Gather round the fire. No? Suit yourself, freeze.", "The square fire's never gone out. Not once. Not even the winter the sea froze.", "Elder's in a mood. Elder's always in a mood.",
			"They hang the midwinter lanterns here. Whole square glows.", "Warm your hands. The fire's free. The gossip costs extra.",
			"Snow sculpture contest at week's end. My wolf looks like a potato."],
		"inn": ["Pull up a stool by the hearth. Seats are for paying folk.", "This round's on whoever came in last. That's you, you're still shaking.", "To the captains! May their fingers thaw.",
			"Mulled cider, a bowl of stew, a seat by the hearth. Heaven.", "Boots off by the door! Snow on my floor means you in the snow.",
			"The fiddler only knows three songs. They're all about the cold."],
		"workshop": ["Sledge runners, bent and pinned. Smell that birch?", "Hold this still. Still. That was my thumb.",
			"Snowshoes for the trappers, six pairs by week's end.", "Bone needles, whalebone buttons. Nothing's wasted up here.",
			"Forge is the warmest spot in town. Swing a hammer and stay.", "Mending an auger. Ice dulls everything, even steel."],
		"field": ["Washing's frozen stiff on the line. Shirts stand up by themselves.", "Shed roof's sagging. One more snow and we lose the turnips.",
			"Stack the logs bark-up. Bark-up! Were you raised on a raft?", "Chop wood and it warms you twice. Once splitting, once burning.",
			"Dried fish on the racks. Somebody's stealing one a day.", "Salt the path to the sheds, or I'll be picking you up off it."],
		"shrine": ["Light a candle for the sailors out in the ice.", "Old gods of the snow. Leave them a pinecone, they're not fussy.",
			"Quiet here. Even the wind takes its hat off.", "Somebody left hot cider on the altar. It's gone. Gods get thirsty.",
			"Pray for a short winter. They never answer that one.", "The crowned figure on the stone was the mountain king, they say."],
		"well": ["Break the ice, drop the bucket, pray it comes up wet.", "Rope's frozen to the crank again. Pass me the kettle.",
			"Water's so cold it hurts your teeth. Best water anywhere.", "Somebody dropped a mitten down the well. Fishing it out.",
			"Morning gossip's at the well. Evening gossip's at the inn.", "Three fingers of ice on it today. Thicker than yesterday."],
		"bench": ["Sit, sit. Bench is cold, but so's everything.", "Heard about the cooper's boy and the goat? Ask me later.",
			"I sit here every day and watch the harbour freeze. Good show.", "The furrier and the brewer are courting. Don't say I said.",
			"My bones creak louder than the ice now.", "Back in my day the snow came up to the rooftops. Now it's only the windows.",
			"Shove over. The sunny end's mine. The only sunny end."],
		"storehouse": ["Grain to the back, fish to the front, rum under the floor.", "Another sack of salt. My back's an old man's back.",
			"Count the barrels twice. The cold makes numbers shrink.", "Stores have to last till the thaw. Every crumb's counted.",
			"Mind the rats. They're fatter than me this winter.", "Pass it down the line. Easy. That's the cider."],
		"pointer": ["If you're after work, {who} {where} has been grumbling about something all week.", "{who}'s got a problem. {who} always has a problem. This one sounded real.",
			"Go and see {who} {where}. Nobody listens to {who}, and that's never ended well.",
			"{who} {where} was asking after a strong pair of arms. Yours'll do.", "Want something to do? {who} is {where}, and very worried.",
			"You'll find {who} {where}. Looked sick with worry this morning.", "Talk to {who}. Last I saw, {where}. Something about a debt nobody's paying.",
			"{who} keeps muttering about the snow eating something. Ask them {where}.", "Ask {who} {where}. Been pacing a rut in the snow since dawn.",
			"If you've coin to earn, {who} has coin to spend. Look {where}.", "Find {who} {where}. Too proud to ask for help, but needs it.",
			"Poor {who}. Saw them {where}, staring at the snow like it owed them.", "{who} {where} swore at a wolf this morning. Then at me. Go and help.",
			"There's trouble with {who}. You'll find them {where}, chewing a mitten."],
	},
	"menu": ["What is it, Captain?", "Captain. Come stand upwind of me, you'll block the gale.",
		"You've the look of someone with questions. Ask, before your lips freeze.", "Well? Speak up. The wind steals half of what anyone says.",
		"Ah, the captain from the ice. What can I do for you?", "Make it quick, or make it by the fire. Your choice.",
		"You again? Good. The town's been dull without a pirate.", "Shake the snow off and tell me what you're after.",
		"Captain! Cold hands, warm heart, or the other way round? What brings you?", "I've a minute before my tea freezes. What do you need?",
		"Go on then, Captain. I'm all ears. Frozen ears, but ears."],
	"work_menu": "So what keeps you busy out here in the ice, then? Life treating you fair?",
	"bye": "Stay warm.",
	"rumour_menu": ["What's the word on this island?", "Heard anything about the islands ahead?"],
	"rumour_isle": {
		"camp": ["They say {name} buried a chest in the snow before making camp. Snow moves. Good luck finding it again.",
			"{name}'s crew raid the store sheds on moonless nights. Can't blame them. Can still shoot them."],
		"beast": ["{name} came down off the mountain three winters ago. It doesn't eat people. It just doesn't like them.",
			"Nobody goes past the ridge any more. {name} snaps pines like kindling. White as the snow, the trappers say, and clever."],
		"lair": ["The bugs in the ice caves click before a blizzard. Louder every year. One day it'll snow bugs, mark me."],
		"ruins": ["The old towers were here before the town. Ice and stone, stacked by someone who didn't want to be found."],
		"lookout": ["Climb to the lookout on a clear day and you'll see three islands. On a bad day you'll see snow, and it's this snow."],
		"any": ["Something's not right out at {name}. Nobody says what. Nobody goes to look, either.", "My uncle went to {name} once. Came back with a story and nine toes. Won't say which he values more."],
	},
	"rumour_chain": [
		"Ships that make it to {name} come back quiet. {blurb}, they say, and meaner than here.",
		"A trader swore {name} has more gold than people. Then he went back, and now it has one more person.",
		"The needle pulls toward {name} next. {blurb}. Warmer than here, anything is.",
		"I've a cousin on {name}. Haven't heard from her in a year. That's normal for her. Probably.",
	],
	"rumour_quiet": ["Quiet island, this. Snow eats sound. That's what my mother says, and she says it about everything.",
		"Nothing worth repeating. Even the gossip's frozen this week.", "Rumours? Snowed under, same as the roads.",
		"I've heard nothing, and out here nothing's good news.", "Ask at the inn. I only know the weather, and it's cold.",
		"Not a whisper. The wolves have been louder than the people.", "Quiet as a frozen bell. Ask me again after the thaw.",
		"My ears have been under a hat all winter. Heard nothing."],
	"rumour_fork": "The sea splits past here: {a}, or {b}. Pick one. The other's never as warm as you'd hoped.",
	"rumour_end": "Past us? Nothing, the old ones say. The sea just ends, and something waits at the edge of it.",
	"rumour_hard": "Harder country than this, mind. Their winters eat our winters.",
	"self_menu": "Tell me about yourself.",
	"accept": "I'll see to it.",
	"decline": "Not now.",
	"taken": ["Good. I'll be right here, by the fire. Probably.", "That's a weight off. Go on, before the light goes.",
		"Truly? Bless your boots. Mind the drifts.", "I knew you had the look of a doer. Off you go.",
		"Then it's settled. I'll keep a mug of cider hot for you.", "Wonderful! Don't freeze, mind. I can't pay a statue.",
		"Ha! A pirate with a good heart. The old ones won't believe me.", "Thank you, Captain. Come back in one piece. Or most of one.",
		"Right. I'll stop worrying, then. Tomorrow, maybe.", "You won't regret it. Well. You might. But not because of me.",
		"Go carefully. The snow up here keeps what it catches."],
	"notices": {
		"board": ["A plank board under a little roof, its notices stiff with frost.",
			"Frost has glued half the notices to the board. The rest flap in the wind.",
			"A notice board, its nails rusted, its papers pinned down with icicles.",
			"Someone's scraped the snow off the board so you can read it. Mostly.",
			"The town board, plastered in notices. Most are about lost dogs and the beast.",
			"Pinned notices crackle in the cold. One's been chewed by something."],
		"bounty": ["WANTED: {name}. Raids the store sheds and laughs about it. Report to {poster}.",
			"WANTED, alive or frozen: {name}, camped in the snow with a crew of thieves. Report to {poster} for the reward.",
			"BOUNTY on {name}, who stole the midwinter cider. Unforgivable. Report the deed done to {poster}.",
			"Gold for the end of {name}, who burned two boats and a fishing hut. Bring word to {poster}.",
			"{name} and crew are camped above the town, eating our winter stores. Drive them off, then report to {poster}.",
			"REWARD: {name}, pirate, for threats, theft and terrible singing. Report to {poster} at once."],
		"lair": ["Something nests in {name}, and it's spreading. Clear it out. Report to {poster}.",
			"HELP WANTED: clear {name} before the clicking reaches the town. Claim the reward from {poster}.",
			"{name} is crawling again. Strong arms and a stronger stomach needed. Report to {poster}.",
			"Our trappers won't pass {name} any more. Burn it out, crush it, anything. Then see {poster} for pay.",
			"Clear {name} and the whole town owes you supper. {poster} owes you gold. Report there.",
			"NOTICE: {name} must be cleared before the thaw, or it'll hatch. Report to {poster}."],
		"beast": ["BEAST: {name} has taken three sheep and a sledge dog. Kill it. Report to {poster}.",
			"{name} walks the ridge at night. Someone brave or foolish, end it, then tell {poster}.",
			"HUNTER WANTED for {name}. Bring proof, a tooth or a claw, to {poster}.",
			"The town will pay for the end of {name}. Report to {poster}, and bring a big spear.",
			"WANTED DEAD: {name}, the terror of the snowfields. See {poster} for the bounty.",
			"Nobody sleeps while {name} lives. Slay it and report to {poster}. We'll ring the bell for you."],
		"posted": ["You did it? Truly? Then this is yours, and the town's thanks with it.",
			"I'll take the notice down myself. With great pleasure, and a hammer.",
			"Ha! I knew someone would. I didn't know it would be a pirate.",
			"The whole town will sleep tonight. Here's your reward. You earned it in the cold.",
			"Done and done. I'll tell the storyteller. You'll be a winter tale by spring.",
			"Here's the purse. Count it by the fire, your fingers will thank you."],
	},
	"service": {
		"inn": ["A bed by the chimney, Captain. Best in the house. Only one in the house.",
			"Rest up. The blankets are wool, the walls are thick, the snoring's free.",
			"Room's warm, stew's hot. Sleep till the sun bothers to rise.",
			"Boots by the fire, coat on the peg, you in the bed. That's the rule.",
			"Need a room? I'll put a hot stone under the covers for you.",
			"Your crew's welcome too, if they wipe their feet. Twice."],
		"trade": ["Furs, rope, lamp oil. Everything the ice hasn't taken.",
			"Got loot? I'll buy it. Got coin? I'll sell you better loot.",
			"Prices are fair. Fair for an island nobody can reach half the year.",
			"Treasure's welcome. Trinkets too. Fish, keep. I've plenty.",
			"That's a pretty piece. I'll give you half what it's worth. Joking. Mostly.",
			"Shot, powder, bandages. Stock up. Nobody's selling past the ice."],
		"cook": ["Fish stew, hare stew, or stew stew. Pick one.",
